meta {
  name: 02 - Needs Review (High Risk)
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/loan/prequalify
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "description": "I make $6500 a month and have been at my job for 4 years. My monthly debt payments are about $800. I'd like to borrow $20,000 to renovate my kitchen. My credit score is 710."
  }
}

docs {
  Rules PASS (nothing disqualifying), but the ML risk score lands in the
  HIGH band -> decision should be "NEEDS_REVIEW", not auto-rejected.

  Expected defaultProbability ~0.536, riskBand "HIGH" (matches the values
  verified directly against the Python gRPC service and the isolated
  Java test during development).
}
